This work introduces new $L^p$ hypercontractive inequalities for the scaled Bergman ball $\mathbb{B}_r=\{z\in\mathbb{C}:\ |z|\leq r\}$. Unlike standard hypercontractivity inequalities, which depend on the mass of the Gaussian weight, these inequalities remain valid across all scales $r>0$. Furthermore, we establish sharp $L^p$ Poincaré inequalities for the scaled Bergman ball applicable to every $p\in[1,\infty)$, determining the optimal constants for every scale $r>0$. While previously derived for $\mathbb{B}_1$ by David and Sibley (2019), those results did not provide constants for arbitrary scales.
\end{abstract}
